## Gotchas

Recurring traps. Add entries when something bites twice; delete entries when the machinery they describe is gone.

- Copier resolves git TAGS, not HEAD. Template updates reach this project only after a new tag; always run copier with `--trust`.
- Verification greps must be case-insensitive and repo-wide (`grep -rni`), or they give a false all-clear.
- Count skills by marker file (`find . -name SKILL.md`), not by directory listing; support directories inflate raw counts.
- In YAML frontmatter, quote description strings containing colons; strict parsers reject them unquoted.

## Session continuity

Before stopping mid-task, write `HANDOFF.md` at the repo root with four lines: current state, exact next step, the verify command, and `git rev-parse HEAD`.
`/catchup` reads it on resume and flags it stale when that hash is no longer HEAD.
Keep it short; when in doubt, the repository state wins over the handoff.

